@flexiarg snatch/forced-play-needs-a-loss-floor
@title Forced Play Needs a Loss Floor
@audience players
@tone cautionary
@style pattern
@why snatch/preserve-the-right-to-abstain
@see-also snatch/ask-for-surplus-not-surrender

! conclusion: When G2 removes abstention, make the compulsory offer no larger than the loss you can absorb.

  + context: **Play grain.** Under G2, P2 has enabled Force Offer and P1 must
    offer despite evidence that the counterpart may snatch.

  + IF:
    Abstention is unavailable and a prior response makes seizure a live risk.

  + HOWEVER:
    An exit-based policy cannot execute in this treatment, but compulsion does
    not make a large exposed offer safer.

  + THEN:
    Offer the smallest permitted positive amount and ask explicitly for a
    reciprocal amount; do not encode an unavailable abstention as the plan.

  + BECAUSE:
    G2 changes the action set, not the cost of seizure. The remaining control is
    the amount placed at risk inside the forced move.
